<title>USA: Starrett sees 1997 EPS exceeding 1996.</title>
<headline>Starrett sees 1997 EPS exceeding 1996.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Starrett Corp said Friday it expected earnings per share for 1997 to exceed the previous year's $0.70.</p>
<p>In a statement, Starrett nevertheless reported a profit of $0.11 per share for the second quarter, half of the $0.22 earned for the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>It blamed rain and restructuring for the low figure.</p>
<p>An official said Starrett, which builds and manages houses and other properties, was optimistic about the year as a whole because it usually did better in the third and fourth quarters of a given year.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
